;; spec:   syntax §4.4, §4.5
;; expect: accept
;; result: 3
;; audit:  clean
;; range takes one or two arguments (Decided, owner, 2026-09-27):
;; (range n) is (range 0 n), and (range a b) the numbers from a up to
;; b. A for-each over a literal range with a literal fn whose one
;; parameter is unannotated becomes a counting loop (syntax §4.4); this
;; fn's parameter is annotated, and a loop variable takes no
;; annotation, so it is the library for-each over the vector (range 0
;; 3) with the closure, which checks the annotation: 0 + 1 + 2 = 3.
;; Before, the library range took one argument and this program was a
;; type error (adversary finding 006).
(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((c (cell 0)))
    (do (for-each (range 0 3) (fn (i: i64) (set! c (+ @c i))))
        @c)))
